4.3.3 The Optimality of Our Construction

This section provides a proof for the claim articulated in Section 4.1, specifically that the encoder produces a sequence c_{k,s} whose length is equal to the upper bound U(k,s). This equality consequently establishes c_{k,s} as the longest possible (k,s)-RdB sequence. To achieve this, the length of c_{k,s}, denoted by ℓ(c_{k,s}), must first be calculated. Subsequently, it is essential to demonstrate that ℓ(c_{k,s}) is equivalent to U(k,s) through a series of algebraic transformations.
